            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0477" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10345: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-01T09:00:00+08:00">October 1, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:03 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Canton River closed to navigation from 6 a.m. today by order of Military
                    Headquarters. While river continues closed Canton-Hong Kong Railway offers only
                    means of transportation between the two cities. It is officially stated,
                    however, that a motor road is being constructed and is expected to be completed
                    soon.</p>
                <p>Hong Kong mail to Swatow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Linnell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
